  "aiInstructionsCopied": "Instructions copied. Paste them into ChatGPT or another AI with the links to your coffees, then share its answer with HolyBeans.",
  "beanAiInstructions": "Prepare coffee cards for HolyBeans from the links and details I provide below. Return one valid JSON object, without Markdown or text before or after it, with one entry in beans per coffee. Keep format and version exactly as shown here:\n\n{example}\n\nSources and unknown details:\n- Read each coffee's page. Use only information explicitly stated on that page or in the bag details I provide. If you cannot access a page, do not invent its contents.\n- The example shows the structure: its names, numbers, dates and other values are fictional. Do not copy them as real data.\n- name must identify the coffee. If you cannot identify it, omit that entry. Omit any other unknown field; do not fill it with assumptions, empty strings or the word \"unknown\".\n- Preserve product names and varieties. flavorNotes is a list of the roaster's tasting notes, not an invented review. shopUrl is the link to that coffee.\n- Write the data in English: countries, processes and tasting notes (for example Ethiopia, washed, peach), even if the page is in another language. Keep the names of the coffee, roaster, region, farm, producer and varieties as the source gives them.\n\nRoast and dates:\n- roastLevel only accepts dark, medium, omni, light or ultra_light, and only when the source states the roast level. An espresso or filter recommendation does not establish the roast level.\n- Include decaf only when the source explicitly states whether the coffee is decaffeinated.\n- roastDate must be an explicit, complete and valid roast date in YYYY-MM-DD format. Do not use today's date, a publication, purchase, expiry or harvest date. If it only says \"freshly roasted\", the year is missing or the date is ambiguous, omit the field.\n- harvest is the harvest stated by the source, not the roast date. Do not add opening dates or freshness calculations.\n\nBag, price and origin:\n- price is the total price of one bag in euros, as a number with a decimal point and no currency symbol. Do not use a price per kilogram or convert another currency yourself.\n- bagGrams is the weight of that same bag in grams, as a number without units. If there are several variants and I have not specified one, omit price and bagGrams rather than choosing one. Do not combine one size's price with another's weight.\n- In origins, use one entry for a single origin and one per known component of a blend, without inventing percentages or assigning details to unspecified components.\n- For a single altitude, use altitudeMeters. For a range, use altitudeMeters for the minimum and altitudeMaxMeters for the maximum, both whole numbers in metres without units. Omit the maximum if unknown; do not copy the example's range.\n- Do not add fields outside the given structure or brewing recommendations.\n\nMy coffees and bag variants:\n",
  "importInvalidJson": "This card could not be read. Check that you copied the complete JSON.",
  "importDroppedTitle": "Some fields could not be read",
